    reviewUrl: "/horizon-7-0-at-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "$1,099–$2,100",
    priceBounds: {"low":1099,"high":2100},
    specs: "20 x 60 in. deck · 0.5–12 mph · 0–15% incline · 325 lb capacity · fan",
    pros: [
      "A full 60-inch deck and 12 mph for about $1,100",
      "Lifetime frame and motor warranty",
      "Garage Gym Reviews’ testers report no shaking during runs",
      "Bluetooth for running apps and Apple Watch support, with no subscription required",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Horizon’s comparison table does not list pace among its readouts, unlike the 7.8 AT",
      "A 20-inch belt asks for a straighter line over a long run than a 22-inch one",
      "No decline, three years on parts and one year of labour",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheapest treadmill we would trust with a marathon block. Spend more if you want decline, a wider deck or a pace readout.",
    description: "The 7.0 AT is the least expensive treadmill here and the floor for serious long-distance training. Horizon lists a 20 by 60-inch three-zone cushioned deck, 0.5 to 12 mph, incline from 0 to 15% and a 325 lb maximum user weight; Garage Gym Reviews’ 2026 review agrees on each, and its testers report the machine stayed steady during runs, sprints and steady-state sessions. The frame and motor are covered for life, which is the most reassuring single fact for a machine that will be asked to run for hours. It has a fan, Bluetooth for apps, Apple Watch support and hydraulic folding. Three things hold it back for marathon work: a narrower 20-inch belt, no decline, and a console whose readouts, according to Horizon’s own comparison table, include speed but not pace. Horizon was selling it at $1,099 against a $2,100 list price when we checked; reviewers note it usually sells near that figure.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Best Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Best Treadmills for Marathon Training", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-treadmills-for-marathon-training/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the best treadmill for marathon training?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For most runners, one with a 60-inch deck, a continuous motor rating with a long motor warranty, a 12 mph top speed and ideally some decline. Of the machines we could verify, the NordicTrack Commercial 1750 fits best, with a 22 by 60-inch belt, a 4.25 CHP rating, -3% decline and an automatic fan. The Horizon 7.8 AT is the pick if you want no subscription; on Amazon, its sibling the 7.4 AT has the same deck and warranty.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you train for a marathon on a treadmill?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, many runners do much of their training indoors, especially in winter or heat. A treadmill is good for controlled pace, practising fuelling and safe running in the dark. Keeping some long runs on the road helps your legs stay used to the surface and the camber you will race on. Our marathon training guide covers how to combine the two.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can a treadmill handle a three-hour run?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "A well-built running treadmill should, if it is maintained. Long runs load the motor continuously, so look for a continuous motor rating and a long motor warranty, keep the belt lubricated on schedule and keep the motor compartment clean. Check your manual for any limit on continuous use, and stop if you notice a burning smell or the motor cutting out.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do you need decline on a treadmill for marathon training?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Only if your race has significant descents. Downhill running loads the legs differently, and decline lets you practise it indoors. Most machines with decline go to -3%, which is enough for gentle descents; the NordicTrack X16, the Aviron Summit and the Sole TT8 go to -6%. For a flat course, decline is a nice extra rather than a need, and the money may be better spent on a wider deck or warranty.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What size treadmill deck do you need for long runs?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "At least 60 inches long, and 22 inches wide if you can afford it. Your stride and position on the belt change as you tire late in a long run, and a short or narrow deck makes you concentrate on staying centred for hours. Taller runners and faster runners benefit most from the extra room. A 55-inch deck is fine for walking and jogging but not for marathon training.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is 12 mph fast enough for marathon training?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For almost everyone, yes. Twelve mph is a five-minute mile, and even a sub-three-hour marathon is run at under 9 mph. The extra speed matters for strides and short intervals, and only quite fast runners reach 12 mph in those. If you do, the NordicTrack Commercial 2450 reaches 14 mph, and Wahoo’s KICKR RUN, sold direct by Wahoo, a four-minute-mile pace.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-10-15",
      dateModified: "2026-10-15",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 6,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/best-treadmills-for-marathon-training/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/best-treadmills-for-marathon-training/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "best");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-10-15",
    modifiedTime: "2026-10-15",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "best treadmill for marathon training",
      "best treadmill for long runs",
      "best treadmill for distance running",
      "marathon treadmill",
      "treadmill with decline",
      "nordictrack commercial 1750",
      "horizon 7.8 at",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Overall: NordicTrack Commercial 1750", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/best/">Best Treadmills</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Treadmills for Marathon Training</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        A marathon block asks a treadmill to do something most never do: run for two or three hours at a time, several times a month, for months. That changes what matters. Here are six machines whose figures held up when we checked them, and the specifications that decide whether a treadmill copes with long runs or just survives them.
      </p>
      <p class="ed-answer"><strong>Short answer.</strong> Best Overall: <a href="#nordictrack-commercial-1750">NordicTrack Commercial 1750</a>. No Subscription: <a href="#horizon-7-4-at">Horizon 7.4 AT</a>. Most Decline: <a href="#aviron-summit">Aviron Summit Treadmill</a>.</p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated October 15, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#nordictrack-commercial-1750"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31BAhBBSPSL._SL500_.jpg" alt="NordicTrack Commercial 1750" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#horizon-7-4-at"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41wMaZFsNwL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Horizon 7.4 AT" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#aviron-summit"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51HkwftQdqL._SL500_.jpg" alt="Aviron Summit Treadmill" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>NordicTrack Commercial 1750 · Horizon 7.4 AT · Aviron Summit Treadmill</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Most treadmill reviews are written around a 30- or 45-minute run, and most treadmills are
          designed for one. Marathon training is different. A long run of two to three hours keeps
          the motor working continuously, heats the room and the runner, and gives you plenty of
          time to notice a deck that is a little short or a console that only shows miles per
          hour. This page names six treadmills that suit long-distance training, says plainly what
          each one gives up, and explains the specifications that separate a marathon machine from
          a treadmill that simply has a big number on the box.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Overall:</span> <a href="#nordictrack-commercial-1750">NordicTrack Commercial 1750</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">No Subscription:</span> <a href="#horizon-7-4-at">Horizon 7.4 AT</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Most Decline:</span> <a href="#aviron-summit">Aviron Summit Treadmill</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Most Speed:</span> <a href="#nordictrack-commercial-2450">NordicTrack Commercial 2450</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Premium:</span> <a href="#sole-tt8">Sole TT8</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best Budget:</span> <a href="#horizon-7-0-at">Horizon 7.0 AT</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[5].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
